# Line endings, diffs, and language statistics, for this repository and for
# every template published from it.
#
# Without the first group, a file edited on Windows enters the index with CRLF
# and stays that way in every checkout afterwards. `text=auto' stores LF in
# the index and hands each checkout the line endings of its own platform, so
# a user on Windows can edit a template without every later diff of that file
# being suspect. After adding a line here, run `git add --renormalize .' once.
* text=auto
*.sty text
*.tex text
*.bib text

# Bibliography styles and figures are not worth diffing or merging line by
# line. `binary' is `-text -diff -merge', so it also keeps them out of the
# normalisation above.
*.bst binary
*.pdf binary

# The venue author kits and their document classes are vendored verbatim: none
# of them is this repository's code, and together they are the bulk of
# templates/paper-cvpr/ and templates/paper-eccv/ by line count. Marking them
# vendored keeps them out of GitHub's language statistics.
acmart.cls linguist-vendored
llncs.cls linguist-vendored
cvpr.sty linguist-vendored
eccv.sty linguist-vendored
*.bst linguist-vendored
